        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261-a4">

                <pb facs="0733" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg611"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Whitehouse to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 20, 1889</date>.
                        (Received October 30.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 148.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your instruction No. 103 of
                    the 9th instant, informing me of the receipt of my telegram of the 8th instant,
                    relative to the punishment of the officers concerned in the outrage at Eagle
                    Pass, and instructing me to inform Mr. Mariscal that Mr. Ryan will confer with
                    him on the subject on his return to this legation.</p>
                <p>I have transmitted your wishes to Mr. Mariscal as directed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Remsen
                    Whitehouse.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
